\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Included papers and their coding. Venue: conference, year and track (Res.\ research, Ind.\ industry/SEIP, JF journal-first, IVR Ideas, Visions and Reflections). Kind: migration kind; A/B means both kinds, and +L marks a legacy source. LLM: role of the LLM (P proposed technique, E evaluated subject, P, E: both; B baseline only, T evaluation tooling, N no LLM (a smaller neural model or no model)). Oracles: letters of Table~\ref {tab:oracles}. Origin of execution-based oracles (Table~\ref {tab:origin}): c:B benchmark tests, c:P project test suite, c:BP both; d:S translated by the system, d:H translated by hand; e:R expected outputs from running the original, e:S derived from the specification, e:U not stated; f:F fuzzing, property-based or symbolic inputs, f:T existing tests or data, f:L LLM-generated inputs, f:C curated samples or screens, f:U not described. Stated limitation: theme of Table~\ref {tab:limits}.}}{21}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:primary}{{10}{21}{Included papers and their coding. Venue: conference, year and track (Res.\ research, Ind.\ industry/SEIP, JF journal-first, IVR Ideas, Visions and Reflections). Kind: migration kind; A/B means both kinds, and +L marks a legacy source. LLM: role of the LLM (P proposed technique, E evaluated subject, P, E: both; B baseline only, T evaluation tooling, N no LLM (a smaller neural model or no model)). Oracles: letters of Table~\ref {tab:oracles}. Origin of execution-based oracles (Table~\ref {tab:origin}): c:B benchmark tests, c:P project test suite, c:BP both; d:S translated by the system, d:H translated by hand; e:R expected outputs from running the original, e:S derived from the specification, e:U not stated; f:F fuzzing, property-based or symbolic inputs, f:T existing tests or data, f:L LLM-generated inputs, f:C curated samples or screens, f:U not described. Stated limitation: theme of Table~\ref {tab:limits}}{table.10}{}}
